## Skills Demonstrated

This project demonstrates:

- Networking fundamentals
- NAT and CGNAT troubleshooting
- Technical research and analysis
- Peer-to-peer networking concepts
- Problem-solving under real-world constraints
- Technical documentation and communication
- Collaborative troubleshooting within a user community

---

## Lessons Learned

This troubleshooting experience reinforced the importance of:

- Understanding NAT behavior in gaming environments
- Identifying infrastructure-side limitations
- Communicating technical concepts clearly to non-technical users
- Systematically narrowing down potential causes during troubleshooting

It also provided hands-on exposure to practical networking issues beyond simulated lab environments.
